\title{Any Equivalence Is a Contractible Map}
\taxon{Theorem}
\import{macros}
\p{
    For every map #{f:A\to B}, there is a function
    ##{
        \mathsf{isEquiv}(f)\to\mathsf{isContrMap}(f).
    }
}
\proof{
    An equivalence has an inverse by [An Equivalence Has an
    Inverse](thm-0016). That inverse can be made coherent by [An Inverse Can Be
    Made Coherent](thm-0018), and a coherently invertible map is contractible by
    [A Coherently Invertible Map Is Contractible](thm-0019). Composing these
    three constructions gives the asserted function.
}
